setuid_hook: handle_setresuid em pr_debug (spam do kmsg)

Um print por setresuid() do zygote a cada app lancado: ~34 linhas/min de
kmsg no S20 (medido no v4.15, 2026-11-16). Vira pr_debug, que sem DEBUG
nao compila. Nao toca uapi nem a versao: o driver continua 33294.
---
diff --git a/kernel/hook/setuid_hook.c b/kernel/hook/setuid_hook.c
index 3184deb2..d0d498c1 100644
--- a/kernel/hook/setuid_hook.c
+++ b/kernel/hook/setuid_hook.c
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ int ksu_handle_setresuid(uid_t old_uid, uid_t new_uid)
 {
     // we rely on the fact that zygote always call setresuid(3) with same uids
 
-    pr_info("handle_setresuid from %d to %d\n", old_uid, new_uid);
+    pr_debug("handle_setresuid from %d to %d\n", old_uid, new_uid);
 
     if (unlikely(is_uid_manager(new_uid))) {
 
